1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,860
Let's settle this with 1 Final Move. Deal?

3
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,300
Whatever.

4
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,620
Ah! My Yo-Yo!

5
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,500
That's the price you pay for destroying my Ice Crack.

6
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,820
I'm Zoe, your old Elementary School Classmate.

7
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,740
Is the Training Camp Cancelled?

8
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,140
The Funding from the School didn't come through in time.

9
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,060
What's going on?

10
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,500
And as for tonight,

11
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:52,380
we're gonna be camping out in tents.

12
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:53,820
Mosquitoes love biting me the most!

13
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,260
If we can't sleep well at night,

14
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,180
our Training during the day will be totally useless.

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Episode 12

16
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,020
Mickey, that's not gonna help.

17
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,710
You're just annoying the mosquitoes.

18
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:16,860
And once you lie down,

19
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,300
they're gonna come back and attack you even harder.

20
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,700
Yeah!
You're driving those mosquitoes crazy!

21
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,590
So I'm just gonna suffer even more?

22
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,580
What am I supposed to do about it?

23
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:24,990
The second I lie down,

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,910
the mosquitoes just start buzzing right in my ear!

25
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:27,900
It's so annoying!

26
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:34,180
Ugh. Well, what do you expect when we don't
have enough funding for Training?

27
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,580
Alright, alright, enough already.

28
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:37,980
Mickey.

29
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,340
Those mosquitoes are already
doing you a favor by just buzzing.

30
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:43,560
For me, I haven't even laid down yet

31
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,660
and they're already biting me all over!

32
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,460
If you guys would just all be like me,

33
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,160
the mosquitoes wouldn't stand a chance.

34
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,780
But doing that makes you look like a Mummy.

35
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:59,100
Hey!
Can't you phrase it a little nicer than that?

36
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,540
Fine, then you look like a rice dumpling.

37
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:03,500
No, more like a little baby in a cradle.

38
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,180
Alright, alright. I actually have an idea.

39
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,620
What's your brilliant plan, Captain?

40
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,940
My brilliant plan is to patiently wait. Just wait.

41
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,340
Wait until the mosquito lands on your skin,

42
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:20,090
and right at the very moment it's about to bite you—

43
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,660
WHAM!
You smack it.

44
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,370
That's so naive.

45
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,460
Actually, what you should do is tense up your muscle.

46
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,340
Then the mosquito won't be able to pull its stinger out.

47
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,260
And even if it somehow manages to escape,

48
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,100
it'll be crippled for life.

49
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,020
Great idea! Great idea!

50
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,980
Oh, and I've also got a bottle of floral water here.

51
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:57,180
Were you planning on giving that to Monica?

52
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,540
Giving her floral water is so old-fashioned.

53
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,420
Sometimes, old-fashioned things are the most practical.

54
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:05,820
And isn't it perfect for right now?

55
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:06,780
Lemme have some.

56
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,100
Hey, I brought you guys some good stuff!

57
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,020
Where'd you get mosquito coils?

58
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,460
Leo took me and Mini

59
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,380
to borrow them from the staff dorm at the Base.

60
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:17,820
Yay!

61
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,310
Tonight, we can finally

62
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,190
get a good night's sleep!

63
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,180
Yeah!

64
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,100
Where's Coach Tony?

65
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,020
Yeah, where is the Coach?

66
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,380
I just saw Coach Tony off by himself,

67
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,340
staring blankly at the river.

68
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:31,000
Huh?

69
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,700
Coach! Coach!

70
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,140
Why aren't you guys in bed yet?

71
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,060
Coach, we just wanted to keep you company.

72
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,460
Coach, mosquito coils!

73
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:22,140
So?
The mosquitoes really bit you guys up, huh?

74
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,540
Mosquitoes? I'm not scared of them now.

75
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,420
Look!
I don't even have a single bump.

76
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,550
All those bumps, and you're still saying you're not scared?

77
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:31,740
My method was the best, wasn't it?

78
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,700
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

79
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,100
The Captain's method was the best!

80
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,980
What do you mean, "best"?

81
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,860
I think my method was pretty good, too.

82
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:42,780
What was so good about yours?

83
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,510
You looked like a Mummy! It was terrifying.

84
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,100
Exactly!

85
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:15,900
Go, Jianghai Team! Go!

86
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,190
Line up!

87
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:22,620
Face Straight!

88
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:25,500
Dismissed!

89
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,620
Chuck, that's your 5th bottle already.

90
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,020
You've used up all the floral oil by yourself!

91
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,940
Have a little sympathy, will you?

92
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:54,300
Look! I'm covered head to toe in mosquito bites!

93
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,220
Didn't we light mosquito coils last night?

94
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,140
Yeah, but they all burned out by midnight.

95
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,540
How come the mosquitoes didn't bite me?

96
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,910
I heard the Captain has some Secret Move

97
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,900
for dealing with them.

98
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,340
So they're too scared to bite him.

99
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,740
Actually, the mosquitoes didn't bite me, either.

100
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
What?

101
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:11,100
Are you guys in cahoots with the mosquitoes or something?

102
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,940
Chuck, I always thought you were the biggest glutton.

103
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,340
I never realized the mosquitoes
were even greedier than you.

104
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,740
Yeah! The mosquitoes knew you went to
the Ancient Town yesterday

105
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,180
and ate a ton of great stuff.

106
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,200
So they've all got their sights set on you.

107
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,940
No wonder I dreamed last night that
I was being carried off by mosquitoes!

108
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,820
I bet that's exactly what the
mosquitoes were actually thinking.

109
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,220
And that thought was transmitted
to you through brainwaves,

110
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,660
and that's how it ended up in your dream.

111
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,580
That's right! Anything that can't
actually be accomplished in reality

112
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,980
it's really easy for it to just turn into a dream.

113
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:38,940
Right, sis?

114
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,820
Mickey, don't just go twisting my words around like that!

115
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,670
I'm not twisting them!
The mosquitoes couldn't carry Chuck away,

116
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,840
so the only thing they could do was enter his dreams.

117
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,060
Alright, everyone.

118
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:50,940
Are you all rested up?

119
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:52,380
Yeah, we're rested.

120
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,300
Then let's get ready for Training.

121
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,500
Right.

122
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,220
Don't forget your stuff!

123
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,580
Okay.

124
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,460
Hey, isn't that the Jianghai Team?

125
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,820
Wow, the villa they're staying in is so fancy.

126
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,220
Tony, I told you before,

127
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:34,470
our Chengnan Team would be
coming here for Training Camp.

128
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:35,750
And you still came here even though you've got no money?

129
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:37,980
Isn't that pushing it a bit?

130
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:39,900
What do you mean, "no money"?

131
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:43,110
We just wanted to experience that "Military Camp" lifestyle,

132
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,270
to toughen ourselves up even more.

133
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:48,060
Alright, stop pretending everything's fine.

134
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,980
When we contacted Falcon Base,

135
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,420
The Management told us

136
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:54,490
that a Team here was already
unable to pay their rent.

137
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:55,740
We had no idea it was you guys.

138
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:00,060
So you're the ones who showed up and threw us out.

139
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,910
Kinda feels like you're just kicking us while we're down.

140
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:03,900
Oh, please!

141
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,300
You overestimated yourselves,
coming here and putting on a tough act.

142
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,700
Let me give you a piece of advice.

143
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,580
There's a bunch of unfinished buildings across the river.

144
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,460
If you stay there, your money problems will be solved.

145
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,440
You don't need to worry about where we stay.

146
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:21,180
Fine.

147
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,580
Well, I wish you the best of luck, then.

148
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,500
Goodbye.

149
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,460
Goodbye.

150
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,500
[Rivals]

151
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:54,980
Coach.

152
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,620
Listen up, everyone.

153
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,060
Don't you worry.

154
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,430
This funding problem will get sorted out.

155
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,340
But I want you all to remember this.

156
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,700
The real showdown is gonna happen on
the Competition Stage.

157
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:09,800
Got it?

158
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,700
Got it!

159
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,860
They came all this way just for Training Camp?

160
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,220
But all they're doing is running.
How stupid is that?

161
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:23,550
They're probably just so
miserable they can't sleep at night.

162
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:25,980
What else can they do but run?

163
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:29,340
Yeah, so pathetic.
Sleeping in tents at night,

164
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:30,780
If they're unable to sleep.

165
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,180
Then shouldn't they be sleeping in a bit in the morning?

166
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:35,580
Unless they're sleepwalking.

167
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,460
And not just one of them —the whole group is sleepwalking!

168
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,350
I'd love nothing more than to run laps

169
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,590
around the Chengnan Team's cabin at night,

170
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,260
just to give them nightmares.

171
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:57,660
That's such a stupid idea.

172
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,060
I think we should just run up to their cabin

173
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,500
and blow a whistle nonstop.

174
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,380
Why bother wearing ourselves out by running?

175
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,780
If the Coach hadn't given us strict orders,

176
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,660
I would've dragged Jacky out to settle this already.

177
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,060
You're the Champion, and he's just the Runner-Up.

178
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,950
And he still has the nerve to come mock us?

179
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,420
Someone needs to teach him a lesson.

180
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:19,260
Let him know that he's nothing more than a Runner-Up!

181
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,900
Chuck, take this seriously!

182
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,740
Captain, I'm so sick of doing these Moves.

183
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:44,850
Can't we do something else?

184
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:48,540
The Coach said these are all fundamental drills.

185
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:51,420
We have to practice them for 2 hours every day.

186
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,380
Keep practicing!

187
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,220
Mickey, put a little more spin into that Yo-Yo.

188
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:59,580
I can deal with their Uniform being old fashioned,

189
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,460
But this training method is just way too outdated.

190
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,380
They're still just practicing the basics?

191
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,260
A whole Team of amateurs.

192
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:11,100
And our Coach still treats them like they're actual Rivals.

193
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,980
She's giving them way too much credit.

194
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,900
They can create their own Signature Moves, can't they?

195
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,780
But what if they can't even come up with any?

196
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:21,180
Their Coach is so weird.

197
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,100
He went through all that trouble
to bring them here for training,

198
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,520
but then he just disappears.

199
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,900
Anyway, all they're doing is repeating the same basic moves.

200
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,780
What do they even need a Coach for?

201
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,780
Oh, I just thought of something!

202
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,060
Their Coach has probably gone across the river

203
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:38,280
to fix up those abandoned buildings.

204
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:42,780
What a joke!

205
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,420
Captain, how can you just let this slide?

206
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,300
Looks like if we don't put Jacky in his place,

207
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:55,950
this guy's never gonna stop.

208
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,620
He's like a fly buzzing around us nonstop.

209
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,540
I was thinking the exact same thing.

210
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,940
But we need to wait for a better opportunity.

211
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,860
No more waiting, Captain!

212
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,300
I'm gonna drag Jacky back here right now.

213
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,740
Chuck.

214
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:09,660
Don't forget what the Coach said.

215
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,580
A lack of patience ruins great plans.

216
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,020
What's there to be scared of?

217
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,420
It's not about being scared, it's just not necessary.

218
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,820
Fighting over a petty grudge isn't the best strategy.

219
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:20,220
The one who gets the last laugh is the real winner.

220
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,180
Exactly.

221
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,100
If the Camp Management catches us causing trouble again,

222
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,500
we won't even have a place left to train.

223
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,900
The Coach's entire plan would be completely ruined.

224
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,020
Is it really that serious?

225
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:30,780
Of course it is.

226
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,220
And you know what I think?

227
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,620
The more they mock us,
the more we should just ignore them.

228
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,500
That'll just prove how pathetic they really are.

229
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:42,300
Captain.

230
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,140
Captain.

231
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,060
You think something's off too, right?

232
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,020
What's off?

233
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,380
Leo is getting more and more manipulative lately.

234
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,780
He's always expressing opinions that contradict yours,

235
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:57,180
and then stirring everyone else up to agree with him.

236
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,730
Don't you think he's got some kind of ulterior motive?

237
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,460
If he likes putting on a show, then let him.

238
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,870
What else can he really do?

239
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:04,860
If you ask me, his next move

240
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,780
is to try and take the Captain's position from you.

241
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,820
And if he really wants that,

242
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,900
there's nothing I can do about him.

243
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:19,260
"Nothing I can do"?

244
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,340
As long as you can handle this,
everything will be fine.

245
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:39,420
Mini.

246
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:42,950
Here, let me carry that.

247
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:43,710
No, it's okay.

248
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,660
Just let me do it.

249
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,390
Are you getting used to sleeping in the tent?

250
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:52,860
Yeah, I'm getting used to it.

251
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,570
Isn't it too tough for you?

252
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,140
It's okay.

253
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,220
There are so many mosquitoes at night.

254
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,810
You probably can't sleep well.

255
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:06,780
Tell you what.

256
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,700
If you don't sleep well at night,

257
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,620
you don't have to do morning practice the next day.

258
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,060
Why?

259
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,900
Is everyone else taking the morning off too?

260
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,780
I'm just worried you're working too hard.

261
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,640
You're the most fragile one here.

262
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,020
And...

263
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,380
And what?

264
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,300
And,

265
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,100
And also...

266
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:40,380
And... you want me to stop talking to Leo, is that it?

267
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,500
Well, thanks for your concern.

268
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,980
But I can't accept that.

269
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,530
Hey, why is the Camp being so nice to us?

270
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:31,740
So many dishes!

271
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,140
How are we supposed to finish all this?

272
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,980
Should we maybe donate some to
a nearby disaster relief zone?

273
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,340
If the disaster zone actually requests it,

274
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,220
we can hold a Special Meeting to discuss it then.

275
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,100
But honestly, those people in the "disaster zone"

276
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,980
look like they're doing way better than we are.

277
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:53,340
I don't think they're gonna need our help.

278
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,860
Alright, everyone dig in! Dig in!

279
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,300
Eat up! Eat, eat!

280
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:13,020
Who are you looking for?

281
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:14,940
I'm looking for Manager Ma.

282
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,830
Manager Ma's not here.

283
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:18,300
What do you need him for?

284
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,190
Who are you?

285
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:23,100
I'm the person in charge of the kitchen.

286
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,500
Kitchen Manager?

287
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,350
Is there a problem?

288
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,340
Well, maybe you can help.

289
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,780
I'm the Captain of the Jianghai Team.

290
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,670
I want to report a problem.

291
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:35,100
Look, even though we haven't
paid the deposit for the next phase yet,

292
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,500
we haven't used up all the meal
fees for this current phase.

293
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,900
So why has the quality of our meals suddenly dropped?

294
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,300
Let me tell you something about this.

295
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:43,740
Manager Ma gave the order.

296
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,180
All those fees for your Jianghai Team's

297
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:48,540
Camping Tents and Training Grounds...

298
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,980
None of those fees have been paid.

299
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,380
So Manager Ma instructed us to take a portion

300
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,270
out of your meal fees

301
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,700
to help cover those other expenses.

302
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,070
Manager Ma's a good guy.

303
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,540
He's bending the rules to accommodate you guys.

304
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,460
So consider yourselves lucky.

305
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,340
If it were anyone else,
you would've been kicked out a long time ago.

306
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:06,780
Hmph.

307
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:12,540
Heh. You've got quite the temper, don't you?

308
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:17,340
Let's stick to the facts.
Why are you making this personal?

309
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,740
If you've got a problem, take it up with the dining hall.

310
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,660
I'm just stating the facts, too.

311
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,820
You guys already lost to our Captain before!

312
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,390
Oh, really?
Then how about you go get your Captain right now

313
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,380
and have him face me?

314
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,780
Don't go running away scared this time.

315
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:34,140
Who was the one who ran away
scared back in the Ancient Town?

316
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,540
Jacky, don't push your luck.

317
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,340
Today, I wanna see exactly who's
gonna be the one running away.

318
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,180
Alright, let's just eat first.

319
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,060
You see that?

320
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:50,940
Your own guys are too scared to face us.

321
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,340
You stop right there!

322
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,260
Who's stopping who?

323
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,660
Coach Sarah.

324
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:02,460
What's going on?

325
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,380
It's Lunchtime!

326
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,780
Why are you causing trouble in the dining hall?

327
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,660
Huh, Jacky?

328
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,060
They started it with us!

329
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:12,990
That's a lie.

330
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,460
You guys were the ones mocking us first!

331
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:17,340
Coach Sarah, it's their own fault their food is bad.

332
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,260
And now they're taking it out on us,

333
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,660
They started saying we were Losers they'd defeated.

334
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,980
Why don't you mention that you were mocking us?

335
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:27,900
You guys are just being too sensitive.

336
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,020
We weren't even laughing at you.

337
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,260
Enough!

338
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,620
No matter who started this whole mess today,

339
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:38,270
I'm standing right here, in front of both teams,

340
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,420
to make this perfectly clear.

341
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,300
We are here to train.

342
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,220
We're not here to pick fights.

343
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,580
What happened today doesn't happen again.

344
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,820
Especially you, Jianghai Team.

345
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,740
Coach Tony isn't here,

346
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:59,100
so you need to be even more
disciplined and stay out of trouble.

347
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:02,980
Because if something does happen,
you won't be able to handle the consequences.

348
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,060
The fight was about to start!

349
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,460
This was the perfect chance to
have a showdown with Jacky.

350
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:29,340
Once he lost, he wouldn't dare act so arrogant anymore!

351
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,190
But of all times, right at that moment,

352
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,660
we got stopped by a Coward on our own Team.

353
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,500
Leo was just thinking about the bigger picture.

354
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:40,350
Matthew was the one who stepped up first

355
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,820
and started provoking them.

356
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,260
We were in the wrong.

357
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,140
No way!

358
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,540
Clearly they were the ones mocking us first!

359
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,940
How are we the ones in the wrong?

360
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,300
Captain, Matthew was the one who provoked them first.

361
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,660
Yeah, he almost caused a huge disaster.

362
00:20:58,300 --> 00:20:59,850
If we'd actually started something in that dining hall,

363
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,000
and something happened

364
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:01,980
we would've been kicked out!

365
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:03,900
And then we'd really be in trouble.

366
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:07,260
I think listening to the Coach is the safest bet.

367
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,660
Matthew, you let your emotions get the better of you.

368
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:13,980
Look, even if Matthew did provoke them on purpose,

369
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:15,420
he was doing it for the Team's pride.

370
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,260
That's way better than someone with no guts at all.

